    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAN AMERICAN GRACE AIRWAYS. ING.\nAMERICAN\nPanagra\nGRACE\nPAN\n*\nAIRWAYS\n*\nOUR\n20,000TH EQUATOR\nDIA DE EMISION\nFIRST DAY COVER\nCROSSING\nPANAGRA\n20,000° CRUCE\nde la\nLINEA EQUINOCCIAL\n25 de Julio de 1951\nPUBLICA\n20.000 Cruce\nLinea\nEcuatorial\nIMBRE\nPANAGRA\nFISCA\n26-Fulio-195 p\nSEREPSSCMEEX\nMr. H. M. Dixby\nPan American \"orld Airways\n135 d. 42nd St•\nNew York 17, N. I.\nU.s. A.",
      "OSTADOS UnIDOS •\n@• COLOMBIA • @CUADOR • PERU • BOLIVIA • CHILO • BRASIL • ARGONTINA\n20,000\nPanagra\nis proud to announce its\n20,000 th\ncrossing of the Equator\non July 26, 1951.\nThis important milestone in the twenty-three year\nhistory of the pioneer airline on the west coast of\nSouth America is due in large part to your\nconfidence and\nsupport.\nTHANK YOU!\nPAN AMERICAN-GRACE AIRWAYS, INC.\nLA RUTA DE\nEl pite Americano\nARGENTINA • BRASIL • CH\nILO • BOLIVIA • PERU • eCUADOR • COLOmBIA • PANAMA • eSTADOS UnIDOS"
    ],
